.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt ZZZ 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zzz
.Nd suspend the machine to idle, with hooks before and after
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
suspends the machine to idle until a key is pressed or, with
.Ar seconds ,
until the clock's wake alarm rings that many seconds later, as
.Ql rtcwake -m freeze -s Ar seconds
does; see
.Xr rtc 4 .
Only root may run it.
.Pp
A suspend to idle holds every process but the one that wrote
.Pa /sys/power/state ,
so a service that must act around it does so in a hook.
Before the suspend, each executable file of
.Pa /etc/zzz.d
runs with the argument
.Cm suspend ,
in the order of the names, and after it each runs with
.Cm resume ,
in the reverse order.
A hook that fails is reported, and the suspend goes on.
.Pp
The images with Wi-Fi have
.Pa /etc/zzz.d/wifi :
before the suspend, a station joined to a network leaves it with
.Ql wpa_cli disconnect ,
so that the access point is told at once, since wpa_supplicant could not
answer the access point's rekeys while it is held;
after it,
.Ql wpa_cli reconnect
lets wpa_supplicant join the best known network in range.
The DHCP client keeps the lease through a short suspend that ends on the
same network, and renews it, as
.Xr init 8
says.
A station that was not joined is left as it was.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/zzz.d/
The hooks.
.It Pa /var/run/zzz.wifi
Present while the Wi-Fi hook has left a network that it joins again on
resume.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after the machine wakes, 1 when the suspend failed or the caller is not
root, and 2 for a wrong argument.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr busybox-util-linux 1 ,
.Xr wifi 1 ,
.Xr rtc 4 ,
.Xr sysfs 5 ,
.Xr wpa_cli 8
.Sh HISTORY
The name and the hook directory follow Void Linux's
.Nm .
